{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/oxidation-reduction/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/oxidation-reduction.html","area":"students","kind":"topic","title":"Oxidation & Reduction | Chemistry","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <!-- Navigation -->\n    <nav class=\"mb-4 flex items-center justify-between\">\n      <a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 transition flex items-center\">\n        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>Back to Electrochemistry &amp; Redox\n      </a>\n      <!-- Progress indicator -->\n      <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n        <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">\n          <span id=\"topic-progress-text\" data-bidemy=\"progress-text\">0% Complete</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"w-24 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full overflow-hidden\" data-bidemy=\"progress\">\n          <div id=\"topic-progress-bar\" class=\"h-full bg-gradient-to-r from-rose-400 to-pink-500 transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </nav>\n    \n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-lg\">\n      <!-- Header -->\n      <div class=\"border-b pb-4 mb-6\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n          <span class=\"mi -exchange-alt text-rose-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"swap_horiz\">swap_horiz</span>Oxidation &amp; Reduction\n        </h1>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Understanding oxidation-reduction reactions, oxidation numbers, and identifying oxidizing and reducing agents.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-rose-50 border-l-4 border-rose-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-rose-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-rose-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>• Define oxidation and reduction in terms of electrons and oxygen</li>\n          <li>• Calculate oxidation numbers for elements in compounds</li>\n          <li>• Identify oxidizing and reducing agents in reactions</li>\n          <li>• Balance simple redox equations</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Section 1: Definitions -->\n      <section id=\"section-1\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-rose-100 text-rose-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n          What are Oxidation and Reduction?\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\"><strong class=\"text-rose-600\">Oxidation-Reduction (Redox) reactions</strong> are reactions that involve the transfer of electrons between substances. These reactions always occur together - when one substance loses electrons, another must gain them.</p>\n          \n          <!-- The Classic Mnemonic -->\n          <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200 mb-4\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2 text-yellow-500\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Remember: OIL RIG</h4>\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n              <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                <p class=\"font-bold text-rose-600 text-lg\">OIL</p>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>O</strong>xidation <strong>I</strong>s <strong>L</strong>oss (of electrons)</p>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                <p class=\"font-bold text-blue-600 text-lg\">RIG</p>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>R</strong>eduction <strong>I</strong>s <strong>G</strong>ain (of electrons)</p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Two Definitions Table -->\n        <div class=\"bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4\">\n          <table class=\"w-full text-sm\">\n            <thead class=\"bg-gray-100\">\n              <tr>\n                <th class=\"p-3 text-left font-semibold text-gray-700\">Definition</th>\n                <th class=\"p-3 text-left font-semibold text-rose-600\">Oxidation</th>\n                <th class=\"p-3 text-left font-semibold text-blue-600\">Reduction</th>\n              </tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr class=\"border-t\">\n                <td class=\"p-3 font-medium text-gray-600\">In terms of electrons</td>\n                <td class=\"p-3 text-rose-700\">Loss of electrons</td>\n                <td class=\"p-3 text-blue-700\">Gain of electrons</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"border-t bg-gray-50\">\n                <td class=\"p-3 font-medium text-gray-600\">In terms of oxygen</td>\n                <td class=\"p-3 text-rose-700\">Gain of oxygen</td>\n                <td class=\"p-3 text-blue-700\">Loss of oxygen</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"border-t\">\n                <td class=\"p-3 font-medium text-gray-600\">In terms of hydrogen</td>\n                <td class=\"p-3 text-rose-700\">Loss of hydrogen</td>\n                <td class=\"p-3 text-blue-700\">Gain of hydrogen</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"border-t bg-gray-50\">\n                <td class=\"p-3 font-medium text-gray-600\">Oxidation number</td>\n                <td class=\"p-3 text-rose-700\">Increases (becomes more positive)</td>\n                <td class=\"p-3 text-blue-700\">Decreases (becomes more negative)</td>\n              </tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Example -->\n        <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -flask mr-2\" data-mi=\"science\">science</span>Example: Reaction of Magnesium with Oxygen</h4>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg font-mono text-center text-lg mb-2\">\n            2Mg + O<sub>2</sub> → 2MgO\n          </div>\n          <ul class=\"text-green-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n            <li>• <strong>Magnesium</strong>: Loses electrons (oxidized) - oxidation number changes from 0 to +2</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Oxygen</strong>: Gains electrons (reduced) - oxidation number changes from 0 to -2</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 2: Oxidation Numbers -->\n      <section id=\"section-2\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-rose-100 text-rose-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n          Oxidation Numbers\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">An <strong>oxidation number</strong> (or oxidation state) is a number assigned to an element in a compound that represents the number of electrons lost or gained by an atom of that element.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3\">Rules for Assigning Oxidation Numbers:</h4>\n            <ol class=\"list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 text-sm\">\n              <li>Elements in their free state have an oxidation number of <strong class=\"text-rose-600\">0</strong> (e.g., O<sub>2</sub>, Fe, Cl<sub>2</sub>)</li>\n              <li>For monatomic ions, oxidation number = charge (e.g., Na<sup>+</sup> = +1, Cl<sup>-</sup> = -1)</li>\n              <li><strong class=\"text-blue-600\">Oxygen</strong> is usually <strong>-2</strong> (except in peroxides where it's -1)</li>\n              <li><strong class=\"text-blue-600\">Hydrogen</strong> is usually <strong>+1</strong> (except in metal hydrides where it's -1)</li>\n              <li>The sum of oxidation numbers in a neutral compound = <strong>0</strong></li>\n              <li>The sum of oxidation numbers in a polyatomic ion = <strong>charge of ion</strong></li>\n              <li>Group 1 metals = <strong>+1</strong>, Group 2 metals = <strong>+2</strong></li>\n              <li>Halogens are usually <strong>-1</strong> (unless bonded to a more electronegative element)</li>\n            </ol>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-rose-50 text-left font-semibold text-rose-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-rose-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2 text-rose-500\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Worked Example: Find the oxidation number of S in H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub></span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-rose-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Let the oxidation number of S be <em>x</em></p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Set up the equation (sum = 0 for neutral compound)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-rose-700 font-mono mt-1\">2(+1) + x + 4(-2) = 0</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-xs mt-1\">H is +1, O is -2</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Solve for x</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-rose-700 font-mono mt-1\">2 + x - 8 = 0</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-rose-700 font-mono mt-1\">x - 6 = 0</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-rose-700 font-mono mt-1\">x = +6</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-green-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                  <p class=\"text-green-800 font-semibold\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>Answer: The oxidation number of S in H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub> is <strong>+6</strong></p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 3: Oxidizing and Reducing Agents -->\n      <section id=\"section-3\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-rose-100 text-rose-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n          Oxidizing and Reducing Agents\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-red-200\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-red-800 mb-3 flex items-center\">\n              <span class=\"mi -arrow-down mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_downward\">arrow_downward</span>Oxidizing Agent\n            </h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-red-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n              <li>• <strong>Causes oxidation</strong> in another substance</li>\n              <li>• <strong>Gets reduced</strong> itself (gains electrons)</li>\n              <li>• Accepts electrons from other species</li>\n              <li>• Oxidation number decreases</li>\n            </ul>\n            <div class=\"mt-3 bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\">\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Examples:</p>\n              <p class=\"text-red-600 font-semibold\">O<sub>2</sub>, Cl<sub>2</sub>, H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub>, KMnO<sub>4</sub>, K<sub>2</sub>Cr<sub>2</sub>O<sub>7</sub></p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-3 flex items-center\">\n              <span class=\"mi -arrow-up mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_upward\">arrow_upward</span>Reducing Agent\n            </h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-blue-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n              <li>• <strong>Causes reduction</strong> in another substance</li>\n              <li>• <strong>Gets oxidized</strong> itself (loses electrons)</li>\n              <li>• Donates electrons to other species</li>\n              <li>• Oxidation number increases</li>\n            </ul>\n            <div class=\"mt-3 bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\">\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Examples:</p>\n              <p class=\"text-blue-600 font-semibold\">H<sub>2</sub>, C, CO, SO<sub>2</sub>, Metals (Zn, Fe, Mg)</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Memory Tip -->\n        <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -brain mr-2\" data-mi=\"psychology\">psychology</span>Memory Tip</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">An <strong class=\"text-red-600\">oxidizing agent</strong> is the one that gets <strong class=\"text-red-600\">reduced</strong>. A <strong class=\"text-blue-600\">reducing agent</strong> is the one that gets <strong class=\"text-blue-600\">oxidized</strong>. It sounds backwards, but think: \"An oxidizing agent does the oxidizing to others, so it gets reduced itself!\"</p>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 4: Video Explanation -->\n      <section id=\"section-4\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-rose-100 text-rose-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n          Video: Understanding Redox Reactions\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n          <div class=\"video-container\">\n            <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/9JIqRhJxpzU\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 5: Practice Problems -->\n      <section id=\"section-5\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-rose-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n          Practice Problems\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. What is the oxidation number of Mn in KMnO<sub>4</sub>?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>K = +1, O = -2</p>\n                <p class=\"font-mono\">(+1) + x + 4(-2) = 0</p>\n                <p class=\"font-mono\">1 + x - 8 = 0</p>\n                <p class=\"font-mono\">x = <strong>+7</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. In the reaction: CuO + H<sub>2</sub> → Cu + H<sub>2</sub>O</p>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">Identify: (a) What is oxidized? (b) What is reduced? (c) The oxidizing agent (d) The reducing agent</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>(a) <strong>H<sub>2</sub></strong> is oxidized (oxidation number: 0 → +1)</p>\n                <p>(b) <strong>Cu</strong> in CuO is reduced (oxidation number: +2 → 0)</p>\n                <p>(c) <strong>CuO</strong> is the oxidizing agent</p>\n                <p>(d) <strong>H<sub>2</sub></strong> is the reducing agent</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. Find the oxidation number of Cr in Cr<sub>2</sub>O<sub>7</sub><sup>2-</sup></p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>O = -2, charge of ion = -2</p>\n                <p class=\"font-mono\">2x + 7(-2) = -2</p>\n                <p class=\"font-mono\">2x - 14 = -2</p>\n                <p class=\"font-mono\">2x = 12</p>\n                <p class=\"font-mono\">x = <strong>+6</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 6: Key Takeaways -->\n      <section id=\"section-6\" class=\"mb-8\">\n      <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-rose-50 to-pink-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-rose-200\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-rose-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-rose-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n          <li>• <strong>OIL RIG</strong>: Oxidation Is Loss, Reduction Is Gain (of electrons)</li>\n          <li>• Redox reactions always occur together - electrons lost = electrons gained</li>\n          <li>• Oxidizing agents get reduced; Reducing agents get oxidized</li>\n          <li>• Oxidation numbers help track electron transfer</li>\n          <li>• The sum of oxidation numbers equals the charge of the species</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Complete Topic Button -->\n      <div class=\"mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200\">\n        <div class=\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"text-center sm:text-left\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800\">Ready to Complete?</h3>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">View all sections, then take the quiz to mark this topic as complete.</p>\n          </div>\n          <button id=\"topic-complete-btn\" disabled=\"\" class=\"px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-gray-300 text-gray-500 cursor-not-allowed opacity-50 flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-medium\">\n            <span class=\"mi -lock mr-2\" data-mi=\"lock\">lock</span>\n            <span>Complete (0% viewed)</span>\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n\n  \n\n  <!-- Topic Tracking and Quiz System -->\n  \n\n\n<div data-bidemy=\"quiz\"></div>","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-rose-50 to-pink-100 p-4 md:p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif}\n    .content-card{-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(12px);backdrop-filter:blur(12px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.95);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);} \n    .accordion-content{max-height:0;overflow:hidden;transition:max-height 0.3s ease-out;}\n    .accordion-content.open{max-height:2000px;}\n    .step-card{transition:all 0.2s ease;}\n    .step-card:hover{transform:translateX(4px);}\n    .simulation-container{position:relative;width:100%;height:450px;overflow:hidden;border-radius:8px;background:#f9fafb;}\n    .simulation-container iframe{width:100%;height:100%;border:none;}\n    .video-container{position:relative;width:100%;padding-bottom:56.25%;height:0;overflow:hidden;border-radius:8px;background:#f9fafb;}\n    .video-container iframe{position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;border:none;}"],"quiz":{"topicId":"oxidation-reduction","subject":"chemistry","passingScore":60,"questions":[{"question":"What does OIL RIG stand for?","options":["Oxidation Is Loss, Reduction Is Gain","Oxygen In Loss, Reduction In Gain","Only Ions Lose, Rarely Ions Gain","Oxidation Increases, Reduction Gains"],"correct":0,"explanation":"OIL RIG is a mnemonic: Oxidation Is Loss (of electrons), Reduction Is Gain (of electrons)."},{"question":"In the reaction 2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO, what happens to magnesium?","options":["It is reduced","It is oxidized","It gains electrons","Its oxidation number decreases"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Magnesium loses electrons (oxidation number changes from 0 to +2), so it is oxidized."},{"question":"What is the oxidation number of sulfur in H₂SO₄?","options":["+4","+6","-2","+2"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Using the rules: H = +1, O = -2. So 2(+1) + S + 4(-2) = 0 → S = +6"},{"question":"An oxidizing agent:","options":["Causes reduction in another substance","Gets oxidized itself","Loses electrons","Causes oxidation in another substance"],"correct":3,"explanation":"An oxidizing agent causes oxidation in another substance by accepting electrons (getting reduced itself)."},{"question":"What is the oxidation number of Cr in Cr₂O₇²⁻?","options":["+4","+6","+7","+3"],"correct":1,"explanation":"2x + 7(-2) = -2 → 2x - 14 = -2 → x = +6"},{"question":"In the reaction CuO + H₂ → Cu + H₂O, which is the reducing agent?","options":["CuO","Cu","H₂","H₂O"],"correct":2,"explanation":"H₂ is oxidized (0 → +1), so it is the reducing agent. It causes reduction of CuO."},{"question":"Which element has an oxidation number of 0?","options":["O in H₂O","Na in NaCl","N in N₂","Fe in Fe₂O₃"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Elements in their free/elemental state (like N₂ gas) have an oxidation number of 0."},{"question":"The sum of oxidation numbers in a neutral compound equals:","options":["The number of atoms","The charge of the cation","Zero","The number of electrons transferred"],"correct":2,"explanation":"For any neutral compound, the sum of all oxidation numbers must equal zero."}]},"tracker":{"topicId":"oxidation-reduction","topicTitle":"Oxidation & Reduction","subject":"chemistry","sections":["section-1","section-2","section-3","section-4","section-5","section-6"],"quizRequired":true},"links":[]}